   "unmapped": [
    "Feedback is a biased noisy gradient oracle: learner chooses tolerance delta; bias <= C_1 delta^p (type-I: gradient bias; type-II: unbiased gradient of a surrogate within C_1 delta^p in sup norm), variance <= C_2 delta^{-q}",
    "the learner knows C_1, C_2, p, q and the Bregman diameter D of the regularizer",
    "K bounded convex body"
   ],
   "definition_quote": "We say that $\\gamma$ is a  $(c_1,c_2)$ type-I oracle for $\\cF$, if for any function $f\\in \\cF$, $x\\in \\cK,0<\\delta\\le 1$, $\\gamma$ returns random elements  $G\\in \\R^d$ and  $Y\\in \\cK$ such that $\\norm{x-Y}\\le \\delta$ almost surely (a.s.) and ... $\\norm{ \\EE{G}  - \\nabla f(x)  }_* \\le c_1(\\delta) $ (bias); and $\\EE{\\norm{ G -  \\EE{G} }_*^2} \\le c_2(\\delta)$ (variance)."
  },
